                <pb facs="0191" n="77" sameAs="frus:frus1922v02/pg77"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">839.00/2659a: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in the
                        Dominican Republic</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Russell</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-11-28T19:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 28,
                                1922—7 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>30. From Welles.</p>
                <p>Please advise Department by cable whether Election Law has been promulgated by
                    the Provisional Government, and if not, probable date of such promulgation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
